                        "reasoning": "The code performs authorization based on a hardcoded string check ('tom') and then relies on a client-provided 'url' parameter to determine if the user is accessing their own profile. While it checks if the URL matches the authenticated user ID, the logic is fundamentally flawed because it trusts the client to provide a URL that it then validates against the session. In a real-world scenario, this pattern is often used to demonstrate how an attacker can manipulate parameters to bypass access controls if the server-side logic is not strictly enforcing ownership of the requested resource independently of user-supplied input.",
