                        "reasoning": "The class `WebWolfUser` implements `UserDetails` and delegates security-critical methods (isAccountNonExpired, isAccountNonLocked, etc.) to a transient `User` object. This `user` object is initialized in the constructor via `createUser()`, but because it is marked `@Transient`, it will not be persisted or automatically re-initialized when the entity is loaded from the database by JPA/Hibernate. If an instance is retrieved from the database, `this.user` will be null, leading to a `NullPointerException` when Spring Security calls these methods during authentication or authorization checks. This results in a Denial of Service (DoS) for the authentication process.",
